The sky130_efx_lvdig standard cells are an independent re-implementation of
cells from the SkyWater SKY130 high-density standard cell library. It includes
or is derived from the third-party work below, all under the Apache License 2.0.

1. SkyWater sky130_fd_sc_hd standard cell library
   Copyright 2020 The SkyWater PDK Authors
   https://github.com/google/skywater-pdk-libs-sky130_fd_sc_hd
   Used: the cells' names and functions, pin names, and transistor-level
   netlists (as installed by open_pdks in
   libs.ref/sky130_fd_sc_hd/spice/sky130_fd_sc_hd.spice).
   Derived from them: the schematics (xschem/sky130_efx_lvdig__*.sch), written
   from those netlists' topology, series order and device sizes, with widths
   (and conb_1's resistor lengths) snapped to the lambda grid, and the library
   netlists built from the schematics and layouts (cdl/, spice/).
   Not used: the layouts in mag/ were drawn independently on the efx lambda
   grid, with no hd layout geometry.

2. xschem_sky130 symbol library (sky130_stdcells)
   Copyright 2022 Stefan Frederik Schippers
   https://github.com/StefanSchippers/xschem_sky130
   The cell symbols xschem/sky130_efx_lvdig__*.sym are modified copies of
   libs.tech/xschem/sky130_stdcells/<cell>.sym (they describe the
   sky130_fd_sc_hd cell interfaces). Each keeps its original copyright and
   license header and carries a note of the changes.

3. SkyWater SKY130 PDK documentation
   Copyright The SkyWater PDK Authors
   https://github.com/google/skywater-pdk (documentation sources)
   doc/cells_skywater.md is a copy of the documentation's list of cells in
   sky130_fd_sc_hd, taken from an unofficial build of that documentation:
   https://sky130-unofficial.readthedocs.io/en/latest/contents/libraries/sky130_fd_sc_hd/README.html
   (the page states no license of its own). Converted to Markdown, with
   "Delay flop" written "D flip-flop".

SkyWater and SKY130 are names of SkyWater Technology. Their use here describes
the process and the library the cells are based on, and implies no
endorsement.
